{
    "$schema": "https://docs.renovatebot.com/renovate-schema.json",

    // This repo is public. Mend does not apply the org config (aignostics/renovate-config,
    // org-inherited-config.json) to public repos, so this file holds the parts of it that this repo
    // needs. Copied from aignostics/renovate-config@33fd3bc1888f. Left out:
    //   - onboardingPrTitle: a global option. A repo config cannot set it.
    //   - hostRules: they use {{ secrets.* }} from the Mend org settings. If a secret is not found,
    //     Renovate stops with a config error. This repo uses no private registry.
    //   - customManagers, except manager-03-version-string: the workflows annotate the uv version
    //     with "# renovate:". No file has a container image or "_renovate" annotation, and the
    //     repo has no Terraform or Terragrunt files.
    //   - packageRules for the other custom managers, kustomize, registry mirrors, git-tags, npm,
    //     Terraform and Cloud SQL: this repo has no dependency that they match.
    // The rules of this repo are in the two sections marked "Repo rules". To update the copy, compare
    // everything else with the new org config.
    "extends": ["config:best-practices"],
    "timezone": "Europe/Berlin",
    "minimumReleaseAge": "5 days",

    // Conventional Commits for every Renovate commit and PR title. Org rulesets reject a PR whose
    // commits do not match "<type>: <lowercase description>", and a squash merge uses the PR title
    // as the commit message.
    "semanticCommits": "enabled",

    // Query osv.dev for CVEs in all tracked dependencies and raise immediate fix PRs when a
    // vulnerability is found. The Dependency Dashboard shows all known CVEs, including ones that
    // already have an open Renovate PR. The dashboard is an issue, so issues must stay on in the
    // repo settings.
    // https://docs.renovatebot.com/configuration-options/#osvvulnerabilityalerts
    "osvVulnerabilityAlerts": true,
    // Renovate 44.232.0 moved the flat dependencyDashboard* options into this object.
    // https://docs.renovatebot.com/configuration-options/#dependencydashboard
    "dependencyDashboard": { "osvVulnerabilitySummary": "all" },

    // A vulnerability fix PR skips the 5-day wait by design, so the fixed version can be hours old.
    // Label it, say so in the body, and keep automerge off, so a person checks the fix before the merge.
    // Renovate ignores schedule and PR limits for these PRs, that is intended.
    // The note goes in prHeader, not prBodyNotes: Renovate applies vulnerabilityAlerts as `force`,
    // which replaces keys instead of merging them, so a prBodyNotes here drops the advisory text
    // Renovate puts in prBodyNotes.
    // https://docs.renovatebot.com/configuration-options/#vulnerabilityalerts
    "vulnerabilityAlerts": {
        "addLabels": ["security"],
        "automerge": false,
        "prHeader": "> [!IMPORTANT]\n> **Security fix, opened without the 5-day wait**\n>\n> Renovate opened this PR because a published advisory affects the current version. It skipped the [**minimum release age** (`minimumReleaseAge`)](https://docs.renovatebot.com/key-concepts/minimum-release-age/) check, so the fixed version might be younger than 5 days. Read the advisory below, check the release age and the upstream release, then merge by hand.\n>\n> uv still applies its own 5-day wait (`exclude-newer` in `pyproject.toml`), and Renovate does not override it. If the fixed version is younger than 5 days, `uv.lock` in this PR is unchanged or the lock update failed. To take the fix early, add the package to `exclude-newer-package` under `[tool.uv]` in `pyproject.toml`, run `uv lock --upgrade-package '<package>==<fixed version>'` and push to this branch. A plain `uv lock` keeps the locked version. Remove the entry when the version is older than 5 days.\n>\n> This exception is configured in [aignostics/renovate-config](https://github.com/aignostics/renovate-config/blob/main/org-inherited-config.json)."
    },
    // Repo rule: the uv paragraph of prHeader is not in the org config. It is here, not in a "Repo
    // rules" section, because vulnerabilityAlerts replaces keys and cannot be split.

    // Release-age wait. Every update waits minimumReleaseAge (above) before its PR exists, so a
    // compromised release is caught by others first. The three keys below open the PR on the day
    // the wait is over and hold releases Renovate cannot date.
    //
    // The PR opens as soon as the branch exists. "not-pending" would hold it another
    // prNotPendingHours: our CI runs on pull_request only, and Renovate does not count its own
    // stability check towards the branch status, so a fresh branch is never "not pending".
    // https://docs.renovatebot.com/configuration-options/#prcreation
    "prCreation": "immediate",

    // Create the branch only once a release has passed minimumReleaseAge, with the newest such
    // release. The PR then appears on the day the wait is over, already green, and never moves
    // down to an older release.
    // https://docs.renovatebot.com/configuration-options/#internalchecksfilter
    "internalChecksFilter": "strict",

    // A release without a registry timestamp counts as too young and gets no PR. A package rule
    // near the end opens these PRs anyway, with the no-release-timestamp label and a note, and
    // turns automerge off, so a person checks the release by hand.
    // https://docs.renovatebot.com/configuration-options/#minimumreleaseagebehaviour
    "minimumReleaseAgeBehaviour": "timestamp-required",

    // Label every Renovate PR with "renovate" plus its manager, so PRs are filterable and
    // self-describing regardless of ecosystem. addLabels is additive: it merges with any
    // labels set by packageRules.
    // https://docs.renovatebot.com/configuration-options/#addlabels
    "addLabels": ["renovate", "{{{manager}}}"],

    // Enable GitHub native auto-merge on every Renovate PR except majors (see the last packageRule).
    // GitHub fires the merge automatically
    // once all branch-protection requirements are met (checks green + CODEOWNERS approval).
    // Requires "Allow auto-merge" enabled in repo Settings -> General.
    // https://docs.renovatebot.com/configuration-options/#platformautomerge
    "automerge": true,
    "automergeStrategy": "squash",

    // Default rebaseWhen ("auto") force-pushes every open Renovate PR branch whenever main
    // advances, even when the dependency update itself is unaffected. That resets CI on PRs main
    // didn't actually touch. Rebase only when main and the PR branch genuinely conflict.
    // https://docs.renovatebot.com/configuration-options/#rebasewhen
    "rebaseWhen": "conflicted",

    // Renovate ships the pre-commit manager disabled, so without this it never reads
    // .pre-commit-config.yaml. Hook revs pinned to a commit SHA with a "# frozen: <tag>" comment
    // (the format "pre-commit autoupdate --freeze" writes) would then never get an update PR.
    // The manager updates SHA and tag together, after minimumReleaseAge like every other update.
    // https://docs.renovatebot.com/modules/manager/pre-commit/
    "pre-commit": {
        "enabled": true
    },

    // Custom regex "# renovate:" / "// renovate:" managers to track versions Renovate's
    // built-in managers can't reach on their own -- e.g. a container tag baked into a shell
    // script variable, or a plain version string in a YAML field with no dedicated manager.
    // Any file, any language: annotate the line above the value with a "# renovate:" or
    // "// renovate:" comment naming the datasource (and optionally depName/packageName/etc.),
    // and Renovate will track and update it like any other dependency.
    // See README.md in aignostics/renovate-config for the full annotation syntax and examples.
    // Following: https://docs.renovatebot.com/modules/manager/regex/#required-capture-groups
    "customManagers": [
        {
            "customType": "regex",
            "description": ["manager-03-version-string: Plain version strings annotated with # renovate: or // renovate:. Handles both assignment (KEY=) and key-value (key:) styles for any datasource."],
            "managerFilePatterns": ["/./"],
            "matchStrings": [
                // Supported fields:
                //   datasource=<value>              (required)
                //   depName=<value>                 (required if no packageName)
                //   packageName=<value>             (required if no depName)
                //   versioning=<value>              (optional, default: semver-coerced)
                //   extractVersion=<regex>          (optional)
                //   registryUrl=<url>               (optional)
                //
                // Examples:
                //   # renovate: datasource=github-releases depName=renovatebot/renovate
                //   RENOVATE_VERSION="44.251.0"
                //
                //   # renovate: datasource=npm depName=renovate versioning=npm
                //   RENOVATE_NPM_VERSION=44.251.0
                "(?:#|//) renovate: datasource=(?<datasource>.*?)(?: depName=(?<depName>.+?))?(?: packageName=(?<packageName>.+?))?(?: versioning=(?<versioning>.+?))?(?: extractVersion=(?<extractVersion>.+?))?(?: registryUrl=(?<registryUrl>.+?))?\\n\\s*[^=:\\n]+[=:]\\s*[\"\\']?(?<currentValue>[^\\s@\"\\'#:]+)(?:[\"\\'\\s]|$)"
            ],
            "versioningTemplate": "{{#if versioning}}{{{versioning}}}{{else}}semver-coerced{{/if}}"
        }
    ],

    // ---- Repo rules: they deviate from the org config ----

    // This repo is a fork of Lotfollahi-lab/nichecompass. The Mend app skips forks unless the repo config
    // turns them on.
    // https://docs.renovatebot.com/configuration-options/#forkprocessing
    "forkProcessing": "enabled",

    "packageRules": [
        {
            // The container-tag and version-string regex managers have no currentDigest capture
            // group, so Renovate can't write back a digest for those deps; disable pin/pinDigest
            // updates for them. The container-digest manager already captures currentDigest and
            // produces "digest" updates instead, so this rule doesn't affect it.
            "description": ["Disable digest pinning for regex manager deps without a currentDigest capture group"],
            "matchManagers": ["custom.regex"],
            "matchUpdateTypes": ["pin", "pinDigest"],
            "enabled": false
        },
        {
            // Ensures inline comments always show the full vX.Y.Z tag (e.g. '# v5.0.0') instead of
            // the shortest matching tag (e.g. '# v5'). extractVersion strips floating tags from the
            // candidate list. Regex versioning (unlike versioning:semver) still accepts floating
            // currentValues as valid, so no dep is skipped. Digest pinning is unaffected.
            // Derived from helpers:pinGitHubActionDigestsToSemver (minus pinDigests:true, already
            // handled by config:best-practices):
            // https://docs.renovatebot.com/presets-helpers/#helperspingithubactiondigeststosemver
            "description": [
                "Ensure github-actions inline comments always use full vX.Y.Z semver tags"
            ],
            "matchManagers": ["github-actions"],
            "matchDepTypes": ["action"],
            "extractVersion": "^(?<version>v?\\d+\\.\\d+\\.\\d+)$",
            "versioning": "regex:^v?(?<major>\\d+)(\\.(?<minor>\\d+)\\.(?<patch>\\d+))?$"
        },

        // Workaround: do not let Renovate hold these four update types forever.
        //
        // Renovate checks the release date at the lookup, and again on the branch. On the branch it
        // has no release date for these update types, so under timestamp-required that check never
        // passes (renovatebot/renovate#45236).
        // A digest update with a release date still waits minimumReleaseAge at the lookup.
        //
        // Remove this rule when renovatebot/renovate#46645 is released.
        {
            "description": ["Workaround: do not let Renovate hold pin, digest, pinDigest and lock file maintenance updates forever"],
            "matchUpdateTypes": ["pin", "digest", "pinDigest", "lockFileMaintenance"],
            "minimumReleaseAgeBehaviour": "timestamp-optional"
        },

        // Two rules for an update without a trusted release date.
        //
        // An update without a release date cannot wait minimumReleaseAge, so a person looks at it.
        // The rules test if Renovate has a release date, not which registry the update comes from.
        // Renovate has a release date for a container image only on Docker Hub, so a list of
        // registries is never complete.
        // The mirror rules make Renovate look up a Docker Hub mirror image on Docker Hub, so the
        // image keeps its release date.
        // https://docs.renovatebot.com/key-concepts/minimum-release-age/#which-datasources-support-release-timestamps

        // Rule 1: an update without a release date gets a label and a note, and a person merges it.
        //
        // The rule reads the release date of the version in use, because Renovate sets
        // currentVersionTimestamp only when that version has one.
        // The rule has no update-type list. Every update type can come without a release date.
        // A digest update gets the release date of its tag, so a tag that is not a version has none.
        // The note heading names the dependency, so a reader can tell the notes of a group PR apart.
        // Lock file maintenance has no dependency, so the heading tests the update type for it.
        // An update with no name at all gets "this update", so the heading is never empty or wrong.
        //
        // Example:
        //   redis:8-alpine@sha256:...            release date of 8-alpine   -> this rule does not apply
        //   bitnami/postgresql:latest@sha256:... no release date ("latest") -> label, note, a person merges
        //   ghcr.io/x/y:1.2.3                    no release date (registry) -> label, note, a person merges
        //   lock file maintenance                no release date            -> label, note, a person merges
        //
        // https://docs.renovatebot.com/configuration-options/#packagerulesmatchjsonata
        {
            "description": ["No trusted release date: an update without a release date gets a label and a note, and a person merges it"],
            "matchJsonata": ["$not($exists(currentVersionTimestamp))"],
            "minimumReleaseAgeBehaviour": "timestamp-optional",
            "addLabels": ["no-release-timestamp"],
            "automerge": false,
            "prBodyNotes": [
                "> [!WARNING]\n> **No release date for `{{#if (equals updateType 'lockFileMaintenance')}}lock file maintenance{{else if depName}}{{{depName}}}{{else if packageName}}{{{packageName}}}{{else}}this update{{/if}}`**",
                "Renovate found no release date for the version in use, so it cannot be sure how old this update is.",
                "Do not rely on the [**minimum release age** (`minimumReleaseAge`)](https://docs.renovatebot.com/key-concepts/minimum-release-age/) here. Check the upstream release, then merge by hand.",
                "**Renovate issues and discussions about release dates**",
                "- Any registry: renovatebot/renovate#37196 and renovatebot/renovate#38656",
                "- ghcr.io: renovatebot/renovate#39064",
                "- quay.io: renovatebot/renovate#38572",
                "- mcr.microsoft.com: [discussion #47038](https://github.com/renovatebot/renovate/discussions/47038)",
                "- Amazon ECR: [discussion #44179](https://github.com/renovatebot/renovate/discussions/44179) and [discussion #39344](https://github.com/renovatebot/renovate/discussions/39344)",
                "This rule is configured in [aignostics/renovate-config](https://github.com/aignostics/renovate-config/blob/main/org-inherited-config.json)."
            ]
        },

        // Rule 2: a digest update automerges only for a Docker image. A person merges every other one.
        //
        // The rule turns off automerge only. It does not change when the pull request opens.
        // Renovate has a release date that it can trust for a digest only on Docker Hub. There the
        // date moves when the tag is pushed again. For a git source, the date is the date of the
        // commit, not the day the tag or branch moved to that commit. A tag such as v4 can move to an
        // old commit, so the wait proves nothing.
        // The rule names the one trusted source, so a new kind of digest update is covered too.
        //
        // Example:
        //   redis:8-alpine@sha256:...        Docker image      -> this rule does not apply
        //   actions/checkout@<sha> # v4      digest update     -> label, note, a person merges
        //   golang.org/x/exp v0.0.0-...      digest update     -> label, note, a person merges
        //   actions/checkout@<sha> # v4.1.2  version update    -> this rule does not apply
        //
        // https://docs.renovatebot.com/key-concepts/minimum-release-age/#digest-updates
        {
            "description": ["No trusted release date: a digest update automerges only for a Docker image, a person merges every other one"],
            "matchUpdateTypes": ["digest"],
            "matchJsonata": ["datasource != 'docker'"],
            "addLabels": ["untrusted-release-timestamp"],
            "automerge": false,
            "prBodyNotes": [
                "> [!WARNING]\n> **The release date of the `{{#if depName}}{{{depName}}}{{else if packageName}}{{{packageName}}}{{else}}this update{{/if}}` digest cannot be trusted**",
                "Renovate can trust the release date of a digest only for a Docker image. For a git source, the date is the date of the commit, not the day the tag or branch started to point at it.",
                "A tag such as `v4` can move to an old commit, so the [**minimum release age** (`minimumReleaseAge`)](https://docs.renovatebot.com/key-concepts/minimum-release-age/#digest-updates) proves nothing here. Read the upstream commit, then merge by hand.",
                "This rule is configured in [aignostics/renovate-config](https://github.com/aignostics/renovate-config/blob/main/org-inherited-config.json)."
            ]
        },

        // ---- Repo rules: they deviate from the org config ----
        {
            "groupName": "GitHub Actions",
            "matchManagers": ["github-actions"],
            "separateMajorMinor": false
        },
        {
            "groupName": "pre-commit hooks",
            "matchManagers": ["pre-commit"],
            "separateMajorMinor": false
        },

        // ---- Org config again: its last rule, which has to stay last ----

        // A major update can break the API, so a person merges it. A group PR with one major
        // update in it does not automerge either. Keep this rule last, so no rule above turns
        // automerge on again for a major update.
        {
            "description": ["Major updates: no automerge"],
            "matchUpdateTypes": ["major"],
            "automerge": false
        }
    ]
}
